The occurrence-count implementation is a translation of Section 2 of
"A Polynomial-Time 2-Approximation for Shortest Common Superstring",
OpenAI, September 24, 2026. It is not the complete approximation algorithm.
The vector transfer implementation follows the positive-forward,
negative-reverse argument in the pinned Steinitz manuscript; that argument
credits earlier Chobanyan transference work. The FFT screen uses the
explicit constants and cost model in the pinned uniform Fourier manuscript.

External historical sources retain their own licenses. This project stores
bibliography, necessary paraphrases and precise locators, not their full texts.
Citation does not imply that every external theorem or dependency was verified.

The exact transport fixture follows the three-affine-max construction in
Section 2 of "Sharp One-Third Stability of Brenier Maps", OpenAI,
September 25, 2026. Polygon integration and a finite transport LP oracle
are independently implemented; this is not a proof of the general theorem.

